{"classification":"source-mismatched-delimiter","correction_applied":true,"id":"O007-CORR-0101","math_ordinal":85,"provenance":{"basis":"exact current source-correction ledger row","kind":"source-correction-ledger","source_resource_ids":["O007-RESOURCE-CH23-SOURCE-CORRECTIONS"]},"rationale":"The inverse-image bracket opened before F_{ni} is closed by a parenthesis in the authority, leaving the formula unbalanced.  Closing the bracket before the outer measure parenthesis restores the intended set expression.","record_type":"source_correction","rights_id":"O007-RIGHTS-FREMLIN-DSL","schema_version":"1.1.0","source_locator":"authority/fremlin/source/mt2.2016/mt234.tex:107","source_normalized_sha256":"fbb71eb274beed55cc9447f8f71171b12ead42f8f0d7b9e04dbae3f317a11aa6","source_text":"0<\\mu(E\\cap\\phi^{-1}[F_{ni})","target_locator":"source/id-ID/mt234.tex:111","target_normalized_sha256":"5dd3704c7a7e74da0db17dd72c7e374001cbdcc476ca855db73724257c8b5649","target_text":"0<\\mu(E\\cap\\phi^{-1}[F_{ni}])","unit_id":"O007-FREMLIN-V2-S234"}
{"classification":"source-extra-delimiter","correction_applied":true,"id":"O007-CORR-0102","math_ordinal":195,"provenance":{"basis":"exact current source-correction ledger row","kind":"source-correction-ledger","source_resource_ids":["O007-RESOURCE-CH23-SOURCE-CORRECTIONS"]},"rationale":"The displayed composition identity has one unmatched closing parenthesis after the argument of the image measure.  Removing it restores balanced application syntax and agrees with the preceding and following lines.","record_type":"source_correction","rights_id":"O007-RIGHTS-FREMLIN-DSL","schema_version":"1.1.0","source_locator":"authority/fremlin/source/mt2.2016/mt234.tex:257","source_normalized_sha256":"edfae7c7da8150743726a488d706a46a0070c611810f803a784896a70756cf61","source_text":"(\\mu\\phi^{-1})(\\psi^{-1}[G]))","target_locator":"source/id-ID/mt234.tex:265","target_normalized_sha256":"2b6a10d9eba1a2fb14d29050fd78c7d39796a6c96b9af224e6f5b8c4dafe34fd","target_text":"(\\mu\\phi^{-1})(\\psi^{-1}[G])","unit_id":"O007-FREMLIN-V2-S234"}
{"classification":"mathematical-missing-integral-operator","correction_applied":true,"id":"O007-CORR-0103","math_ordinal":291,"provenance":{"basis":"exact current source-correction ledger row","kind":"source-correction-ledger","source_resource_ids":["O007-RESOURCE-CH23-SOURCE-CORRECTIONS"]},"rationale":"The proposition requires the sum of positive-part integrals; without the integral sign the expression is not a scalar and conflicts with the proof in 234H(c)(iii).","record_type":"source_correction","rights_id":"O007-RIGHTS-FREMLIN-DSL","schema_version":"1.1.0","source_locator":"authority/fremlin/source/mt2.2016/mt234.tex:362","source_normalized_sha256":"7ce2aec77ceb058acd71831ccc09b99a1bc72ee674459f3f78760f39bb927356","source_text":"\\sum_{i\\in I}f^+d\\mu_i","target_locator":"source/id-ID/mt234.tex:377","target_normalized_sha256":"7c5dc9429a630a645d384eed2e4288339e956cdb785bd9e26df0f4d3a2a70747","target_text":"\\sum_{i\\in I}\\int f^+d\\mu_i","unit_id":"O007-FREMLIN-V2-S234"}
{"classification":"mathematical-missing-integral-operator","correction_applied":true,"id":"O007-CORR-0104","math_ordinal":292,"provenance":{"basis":"exact current source-correction ledger row","kind":"source-correction-ledger","source_resource_ids":["O007-RESOURCE-CH23-SOURCE-CORRECTIONS"]},"rationale":"The proposition requires the sum of negative-part integrals; without the integral sign the expression is not a scalar and conflicts with the proof in 234H(c)(iii).","record_type":"source_correction","rights_id":"O007-RIGHTS-FREMLIN-DSL","schema_version":"1.1.0","source_locator":"authority/fremlin/source/mt2.2016/mt234.tex:362","source_normalized_sha256":"fc8b78a5f7088e9654aa1d121587beac63794b824f6efd545d76fe9c34519563","source_text":"\\sum_{i\\in I}f^-d\\mu_i","target_locator":"source/id-ID/mt234.tex:377","target_normalized_sha256":"86a04d59b89539d78e2eddccdbe315727a9d8525c29c5823ede31c245cb369ef","target_text":"\\sum_{i\\in I}\\int f^-d\\mu_i","unit_id":"O007-FREMLIN-V2-S234"}
{"classification":"mathematical-undefined-variable","correction_applied":true,"id":"O007-CORR-0105","math_ordinal":302,"provenance":{"basis":"exact current source-correction ledger row","kind":"source-correction-ledger","source_resource_ids":["O007-RESOURCE-CH23-SOURCE-CORRECTIONS"]},"rationale":"Only E and F are introduced in this proof.  Completeness of each mu_i yields E in Sigma_i from E subseteq F and mu_i F=0; no indexed E_i exists.","record_type":"source_correction","rights_id":"O007-RIGHTS-FREMLIN-DSL","schema_version":"1.1.0","source_locator":"authority/fremlin/source/mt2.2016/mt234.tex:371","source_normalized_sha256":"b251cbed3bc7e1fb2954006af3974141472b4f8a8b3adf075cd98d8711f3d5ea","source_text":"E_i\\in\\Sigma_i","target_locator":"source/id-ID/mt234.tex:386","target_normalized_sha256":"eb175f9df9ccdcbf76627baec7ec0cb7b79460c26ea7165e0ddce22bb0a0fa58","target_text":"E\\in\\Sigma_i","unit_id":"O007-FREMLIN-V2-S234"}
{"classification":"mathematical-wrong-interval-endpoint","correction_applied":true,"id":"O007-CORR-0106","math_ordinal":331,"provenance":{"basis":"exact current source-correction ledger row","kind":"source-correction-ledger","source_resource_ids":["O007-RESOURCE-CH23-SOURCE-CORRECTIONS"]},"rationale":"The proposition and the two preceding occurrences concern extended-real integrals on [-infinity,infinity].  Repeating positive infinity as both endpoints collapses the interval and contradicts the equivalence being proved.","record_type":"source_correction","rights_id":"O007-RIGHTS-FREMLIN-DSL","schema_version":"1.1.0","source_locator":"authority/fremlin/source/mt2.2016/mt234.tex:421","source_normalized_sha256":"8a3835fa18eae8459cb4309ddb24500c14a6884f31bc3a7c79f76fd0a0e53069","source_text":"[\\infty,\\infty]","target_locator":"source/id-ID/mt234.tex:437","target_normalized_sha256":"c2786c0b1c91c05fddbf58b2a0b7fcf49f8a8ddf6f76db8508839ae252b71f66","target_text":"[-\\infty,\\infty]","unit_id":"O007-FREMLIN-V2-S234"}
{"classification":"source-mismatched-delimiter","correction_applied":true,"id":"O007-CORR-0107","math_ordinal":620,"provenance":{"basis":"exact current source-correction ledger row","kind":"source-correction-ledger","source_resource_ids":["O007-RESOURCE-CH23-SOURCE-CORRECTIONS"]},"rationale":"The essential-supremum equivalence measures H minus the union of H' and X minus G.  The authority has an unmatched extra opening parenthesis and fails to close the measure application; the corrected grouping is balanced and yields the next equivalence.","record_type":"source_correction","rights_id":"O007-RIGHTS-FREMLIN-DSL","schema_version":"1.1.0","source_locator":"authority/fremlin/source/mt2.2016/mt234.tex:741","source_normalized_sha256":"cf7004aa8a9d3a541ce1d8a337ca1cb2a84a6d5c5feedea9b44b50d1a26ff9a1","source_text":"\\hat\\mu(H\\setminus((H'\\cup(X\\setminus G)))=0","target_locator":"source/id-ID/mt234.tex:757","target_normalized_sha256":"4ec6082e46053d9fe02466e1cd6920260afb2ed1a50cdcca6efd38f128094c32","target_text":"\\hat\\mu(H\\setminus(H'\\cup(X\\setminus G)))=0","unit_id":"O007-FREMLIN-V2-S234"}
{"classification":"mathematical-wrong-reference-measure","correction_applied":true,"id":"O007-CORR-0108","math_ordinal":710,"provenance":{"basis":"exact current source-correction ledger row","kind":"source-correction-ledger","source_resource_ids":["O007-RESOURCE-CH23-SOURCE-CORRECTIONS"]},"rationale":"The theorem assumes that nu is an indefinite-integral measure over mu.  Referring to nu as its own base measure contradicts the theorem statement and the cited consequences, all of which use mu.","record_type":"source_correction","rights_id":"O007-RIGHTS-FREMLIN-DSL","schema_version":"1.1.0","source_locator":"authority/fremlin/source/mt2.2016/mt234.tex:821","source_normalized_sha256":"84eb2b123d1102b8f7c00b34116df32107cffa82d46efbac7fd9543fa7459c38","source_text":"indefinite-integral measure over \\nu","target_locator":"source/id-ID/mt234.tex:840-841","target_normalized_sha256":"492247e1bab15272d1e53b8015c042bf6fa0cb8f23ec52cad93d6ba80dafb804","target_text":"ukuran integral tak tentu terhadap \\mu","unit_id":"O007-FREMLIN-V2-S234"}
{"classification":"mathematical-missing-summand-grouping","correction_applied":true,"id":"O007-CORR-0109","math_ordinal":839,"provenance":{"basis":"exact current source-correction ledger row","kind":"source-correction-ledger","source_resource_ids":["O007-RESOURCE-CH23-SOURCE-CORRECTIONS"]},"rationale":"The equality expands nu F minus mu F term by term.  Without grouping, only the nu terms are summed and a single free n remains in the mu term; parentheses make both terms part of every summand.","record_type":"source_correction","rights_id":"O007-RIGHTS-FREMLIN-DSL","schema_version":"1.1.0","source_locator":"authority/fremlin/source/mt2.2016/mt234.tex:943-946","source_normalized_sha256":"4944431bd767ecdfb7fced87718af3b1c32ff4cc1bd385ffe7384e4def8c7fdc","source_text":"\\sum_{n=0}^{\\infty}\\nu(F\\cap G_n)-\\mu(F\\cap G_n)","target_locator":"source/id-ID/mt234.tex:966-969","target_normalized_sha256":"48a9a0fccdcfa5bdd4dced2bb4aeae4621b6c5c0fb3c33da09d38c64178eb41d","target_text":"\\sum_{n=0}^{\\infty}(\\nu(F\\cap G_n)-\\mu(F\\cap G_n))","unit_id":"O007-FREMLIN-V2-S234"}
{"classification":"mathematical-missing-summand-grouping","correction_applied":true,"id":"O007-CORR-0110","math_ordinal":850,"provenance":{"basis":"exact current source-correction ledger row","kind":"source-correction-ledger","source_resource_ids":["O007-RESOURCE-CH23-SOURCE-CORRECTIONS"]},"rationale":"The finite choice is made from the sum of the differences defining lambda G_n.  Without parentheses only nu F_n is summed and the final mu F_n has a free index.","record_type":"source_correction","rights_id":"O007-RIGHTS-FREMLIN-DSL","schema_version":"1.1.0","source_locator":"authority/fremlin/source/mt2.2016/mt234.tex:953","source_normalized_sha256":"4ded4f81b20556441aba4b59464bac9838b57f95bb8e54d1e662be5b4430e7ef","source_text":"\\sum_{n=0}^m\\nu F_n-\\mu F_n\\ge\\gamma","target_locator":"source/id-ID/mt234.tex:977","target_normalized_sha256":"9077ab446a4fb3464e656c8551789c3c7b565f142178bfab913b4521e836b907","target_text":"\\sum_{n=0}^m(\\nu F_n-\\mu F_n)\\ge\\gamma","unit_id":"O007-FREMLIN-V2-S234"}
{"classification":"mathematical-missing-summand-grouping","correction_applied":true,"id":"O007-CORR-0111","math_ordinal":855,"provenance":{"basis":"exact current source-correction ledger row","kind":"source-correction-ledger","source_resource_ids":["O007-RESOURCE-CH23-SOURCE-CORRECTIONS"]},"rationale":"The equality uses finite additivity for nu F minus mu F.  Both terms must be grouped inside the sum; otherwise the displayed equality leaves the last mu term unsummed.","record_type":"source_correction","rights_id":"O007-RIGHTS-FREMLIN-DSL","schema_version":"1.1.0","source_locator":"authority/fremlin/source/mt2.2016/mt234.tex:957-958","source_normalized_sha256":"1d5ae841c042285a964e9ab04f76a3cbec160b48c2d8c543ae1ccbde85f177a4","source_text":"\\sum_{n=0}^m\\nu F_n-\\mu F_n","target_locator":"source/id-ID/mt234.tex:981-982","target_normalized_sha256":"ee8495725acc17d8d7f8b8dec5e50c5e1f0200e14329e3712dfd5dcee9861f98","target_text":"\\sum_{n=0}^m(\\nu F_n-\\mu F_n)","unit_id":"O007-FREMLIN-V2-S234"}
{"classification":"mathematical-wrong-domain","correction_applied":true,"id":"O007-CORR-0112","math_ordinal":1062,"provenance":{"basis":"exact current source-correction ledger row","kind":"source-correction-ledger","source_resource_ids":["O007-RESOURCE-CH23-SOURCE-CORRECTIONS"]},"rationale":"The exercise defines Sigma as a sigma-algebra on X and then defines mu on X.  Tau is the sigma-algebra on Y, so E belongs to Sigma; using Tau is a type error.","record_type":"source_correction","rights_id":"O007-RIGHTS-FREMLIN-DSL","schema_version":"1.1.0","source_locator":"authority/fremlin/source/mt2.2016/mt234.tex:1160","source_normalized_sha256":"2c51c23a716fda0bf481e7a5326d3f3bfbae2b118b054427c24bebecf5853122","source_text":"\\mu E=\\nu\\phi[E] for E\\in\\Tau","target_locator":"source/id-ID/mt234.tex:1190","target_normalized_sha256":"afe4bbaaedba5158924d3a0bd77f0304472650e71de5aed22515cc3a0a8e1bd2","target_text":"\\mu E=\\nu\\phi[E] untuk E\\in\\Sigma","unit_id":"O007-FREMLIN-V2-S234"}
